  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR changes the header comments and the `description` of `assets/posts/sodick-wire.cps` (\"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)\"). No code line changes.\n\n- The control line now names the control: `(SODICK MARK 21 / EX21 CONTROL WORDS - NOT VERIFIED ON A CONTROL - CHECK BEFORE CUTTING)`.\n- A new line follows it in every program: `(LN1W/LN2W: NOT SUPPORTED - G21 ALARMS E00170 AND THE TAPER WORDS DIFFER - USE THE SODICK WIRE EDM LN2W POST)` (#4046).\n- The threading line now matches the program (#4044):\n  - With AWT: `(PROGRAM THREADS THE WIRE WITH T91 AT START)`.\n  - Without AWT: `(WIRE NOT THREADED AT START - THE OPERATOR THREADS IT AT THE M00)`.\n- The post `description` now reads: \"Sodick wire EDM, 2-axis (Mark 21 / EX21 control, words from the 1998 operation manual; not verified on a control). LN1W/LN2W: not supported - G21 alarms (E00170) and the taper words differ - use the Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W) post\". The text before the first \" (\" does not change. Thus `units::post_name` names the post in a refusal as before.\n\nThe G-code comment has no parentheses around `E00170` and `LN2W`. The first `)` ends a comment on the control. The description is not G-code, so it keeps the given wording.\n\n## Cause\n\n- #4046: the header said \"MARK 21 WORDS\" only. An LN2W owner read it as a post for their control. On LN2W, `G21` gives alarm `E00170`, and taper uses other words.\n- #4044: the header said \"WIRE NOT THREADED AT START\". Some lines later the program writes `T91`, which threads the wire.\n\n## Taper programs (#4046 \"beside the first G74/G75\")\n\nThis post writes no `G74`/`G75` and no taper words. It refuses a tapered or 4-axis section by name (`taper_and_four_axis_are_refused_by_name`, `sodick_taper.rs`). Thus no taper program exists to carry a second line. The header line is in every program, the refused ones too. The refusal messages do not change, because this PR changes only comments and the description. The decision file records this.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pin: `camcraft-post` `sodick_dielectric::the_header_names_the_mark_21_control_warns_ln_owners_and_states_the_threading`. It checks the control line, the LN1W/LN2W line and the threading line before the first code line, with and without AWT. It also checks the description.\n- Red before the fix: yes. On the unchanged post it fails at `sodick_dielectric.rs:218` (\"`(SODICK MARK 21 / EX21 CONTROL WORDS ...)` missing\").\n- Mutation: the post from `upstream/main` put back gives red. The fixed post gives green (8 passed).\n- Expected-change tests in `crates/app/tests/sodick_wire_post.rs`:\n  - `the_punch_contour_posts_its_sodick_golden_through_the_gate` now looks for the T91 line and the LN1W/LN2W line.\n  - `taper_and_four_axis_are_refused_by_name` checked that a refused program has no `T91` text. The header comment now names T91. The check now reads code lines only. The app writes no file for a refused program.\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 144 steps, 0 failed (all `camcraft-post` suites, the 7 Sodick suites included).\n- The quick plan ran only the `camcraft-app` lib, so these app suites ran by name: `sodick_wire_post` (8), `sodick_wire_dielectric` (3), `sodick_wire_passes` (5), `sodick_alc400g` (6), `wire_dxf_selection` (14), `wire_post` (22), `mcp_wire_contour` (10), `conformance` (7), `machine` (33). All pass.\n- Example catalog: `example_catalog` (43 passed, 4 heavy ignored), `example_catalog_adaptive` (1), `example_catalog_edge_work` (1). All pass. No catalog program uses this post.\n- Clippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reaches 71 steps, because the post file is a shared input. I ran the two steps that hold Sodick programs: `app heavy: wire_dxf_selection` (ok, 168 s) and `app heavy: wire_post` (ok, 2 s). This is a P3 PR, so AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" asks for no heavy step.\n- Light lane: not run. Its dry run shows 6 motion and pocket steps. This diff does not touch them.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n8 goldens. In each one, two header comment lines become three. Every code line is byte-identical: a compare of each file against `upstream/main` with the `(` comment lines removed shows no difference.\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_dxf_die_circle.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_dxf_die_circle_arc_lead.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_dxf_punch_fillet.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch_flushed.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch_passes.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-wire/wire_slug_punch_passes_flushed.nc`\n- `crates/post/tests/golden/sodick_comment_escape.nc`\n\nAll 8 use AWT, so each gets the T91 line.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No Sodick control read the new comments. The `/` and `:` in the LN1W/LN2W line are inside a comment. A Mark 21 control was not available to confirm that it accepts them there.\n- The Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W) post is in PR #4065. It is not merged yet. The new line names it before it ships.\n- `wire-iso.cps` has the same \"WIRE NOT THREADED AT START\" line. #4044 is about the Sodick post only, so that post does not change.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #3617 changes `crates/app/tests/sodick_wire_post.rs` in `punch_doc_with` (line 70). This PR changes two other test functions in the same file. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- PR #4065 (LN2W post) does not touch `sodick-wire.cps`.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/4046-sodick-mark21-header.md`.\n\nChangelog: Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21) post: the program header names the Mark 21 / EX21 control, warns that LN1W/LN2W is not supported (G21 alarm E00170, other taper words), and states the threading that the program does (T91 with AWT).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4046\nFixes #4044\n",
